WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.360 --> 00:00:02.070
- Welcome to the Huberman Lab Podcast,

00:00:02.070 --> 00:00:04.920
where we discuss science
and science based tools

00:00:04.920 --> 00:00:05.973
for everyday life.

00:00:09.330 --> 00:00:10.350
I'm Andrew Huberman,

00:00:10.350 --> 00:00:13.290
and I'm a professor of
neurobiology and ophthalmology

00:00:13.290 --> 00:00:15.120
at Stanford School of Medicine.

00:00:15.120 --> 00:00:17.220
Today we are discussing nicotine.

00:00:17.220 --> 00:00:19.890
Nicotine is one of the most
commonly consumed substances

00:00:19.890 --> 00:00:21.660
on the entire planet.

00:00:21.660 --> 00:00:23.760
There are literally billions of people

00:00:23.760 --> 00:00:26.670
that ingest nicotine on a daily basis.

00:00:26.670 --> 00:00:29.700
Most of those people consume
nicotine via smoking,

00:00:29.700 --> 00:00:31.890
and in particular smoking tobacco.

00:00:31.890 --> 00:00:33.660
Tobacco contains nicotine and it

00:00:33.660 --> 00:00:35.940
contains a bunch of other things as well,

00:00:35.940 --> 00:00:37.230
which we will talk about.

00:00:37.230 --> 00:00:39.960
And the burning of tobacco
liberates nicotine and makes it

00:00:39.960 --> 00:00:43.200
accessible to the various
cells and tissues of the body.

00:00:43.200 --> 00:00:45.720
But of course, there are other
sources of nicotine as well.

00:00:45.720 --> 00:00:48.270
Some people consume nicotine through dip,

00:00:48.270 --> 00:00:50.340
that is placing tobacco on the inside

00:00:50.340 --> 00:00:52.860
of the lip or in the cheek.

00:00:52.860 --> 00:00:55.470
Some people consume nicotine via snuff,

00:00:55.470 --> 00:00:57.750
which is literally the
shoving of tobacco leaves

00:00:57.750 --> 00:01:00.510
up the nostrils and allowing the tobacco

00:01:00.510 --> 00:01:03.240
to access the nervous
system and other areas

00:01:03.240 --> 00:01:05.400
of the body by permeating into the

00:01:05.400 --> 00:01:07.740
mucosal membranes, that is the lining,

00:01:07.740 --> 00:01:09.900
the soft lining of the nasal passages.

00:01:09.900 --> 00:01:12.720
And of course there are
nicotine patches, nicotine gum,

00:01:12.720 --> 00:01:14.370
there's nicotine in pill form,

00:01:14.370 --> 00:01:17.190
there are toothpicks dipped
in nicotine, et cetera.

00:01:17.190 --> 00:01:19.890
Today we are going to separate
our discussion of nicotine

00:01:19.890 --> 00:01:22.260
from a discussion of smoking and vaping

00:01:22.260 --> 00:01:24.570
and the other forms of
delivery for nicotine.

00:01:24.570 --> 00:01:27.120
We will be talking
about smoking and vaping

00:01:27.120 --> 00:01:29.520
and other routes of
nicotine administration,

00:01:29.520 --> 00:01:33.840
both for sake of highlighting
their detriments to health

00:01:33.840 --> 00:01:37.560
and, believe it or not, in certain cases,

00:01:37.560 --> 00:01:40.080
keep in mind very specific certain cases,

00:01:40.080 --> 00:01:43.080
the possible health benefits
of delivering nicotine

00:01:43.080 --> 00:01:45.600
through specific modalities.

00:01:45.600 --> 00:01:47.550
Turns out those modalities do not

00:01:47.550 --> 00:01:50.820
include smoking cigarettes or vaping.

00:01:50.820 --> 00:01:53.730
And we are going to pay particular
attention to vaping today

00:01:53.730 --> 00:01:56.340
because vaping use is on the rise,

00:01:56.340 --> 00:02:00.390
in particular in young
people, and vaping use,

00:02:00.390 --> 00:02:03.660
and the fact that most
tobacco that's consumed

00:02:03.660 --> 00:02:06.810
through vaping includes
quite amount of nicotine

00:02:06.810 --> 00:02:09.090
has created a scenario where nicotine

00:02:09.090 --> 00:02:10.590
because of its ability to change

00:02:10.590 --> 00:02:13.770
certain chemicals in the
brain can actually lead to

00:02:13.770 --> 00:02:17.785
addiction for a number of other
substances related to vaping

00:02:17.785 --> 00:02:19.560
and vaping associated behaviors.

00:02:19.560 --> 00:02:21.900
If all of that seems like
a lot to get your arms

00:02:21.900 --> 00:02:24.660
and your mind around right here
at the outset, don't worry,

00:02:24.660 --> 00:02:26.430
I'll walk you through this,

00:02:26.430 --> 00:02:27.870
regardless of whether or
not you have a background

00:02:27.870 --> 00:02:28.980
in biology or not.

00:02:28.980 --> 00:02:31.990
I promise that you'll come
through at the end of this

00:02:31.990 --> 00:02:34.320
episode with a deep understanding
of how nicotine works

00:02:34.320 --> 00:02:36.690
in the brain and body,
some of its benefits,

00:02:36.690 --> 00:02:38.340
some of its potential drawbacks,

00:02:38.340 --> 00:02:42.450
and you'll have clear optics
as to why smoking and vaping

00:02:42.450 --> 00:02:44.970
and other forms of nicotine
delivery have the effects

00:02:44.970 --> 00:02:47.880
that they do on your
biology and psychology.

