00:03:41.880 --> 00:03:42.930
Before we go any further,

00:03:42.930 --> 00:03:45.180
I just want to highlight a key takeaway

00:03:45.180 --> 00:03:48.960
from a previous episode,
which is our episode on focus.

00:03:48.960 --> 00:03:51.840
And in fact was a toolkit for focus.

00:03:51.840 --> 00:03:53.580
So during the toolkit for focus episode,

00:03:53.580 --> 00:03:55.920
we talked about a large number
of behavioral, pharmacologic,

00:03:55.920 --> 00:03:58.770
and another interventions
that you can use to increase

00:03:58.770 --> 00:04:01.560
your level of concentration
and focus for whatever purpose,

00:04:01.560 --> 00:04:04.200
cognitive endeavors, learning languages,

00:04:04.200 --> 00:04:06.630
focusing in school, on work, et cetera,

00:04:06.630 --> 00:04:08.220
or physical pursuits.

00:04:08.220 --> 00:04:10.500
Now one of the key takeaways is that

00:04:10.500 --> 00:04:12.540
there are really two key

00:04:12.540 --> 00:04:15.000
protocols that I believe
everyone should understand

00:04:15.000 --> 00:04:17.130
and know about and why they work

00:04:17.130 --> 00:04:18.540
because they are so effective,

00:04:18.540 --> 00:04:21.270
and also because they dovetail
nicely with some of the

00:04:21.270 --> 00:04:23.400
information that we're
going to talk about today,

00:04:23.400 --> 00:04:25.110
which will explain why nicotine

00:04:25.110 --> 00:04:28.170
is so effective in increasing focus.

00:04:28.170 --> 00:04:30.660
And these two protocols are as follows.

00:04:30.660 --> 00:04:33.810
Data based on studies
done in Wendy Suzuki's lab

00:04:33.810 --> 00:04:35.430
at New York University.

00:04:35.430 --> 00:04:37.980
And of course, Wendy was
a guest on this podcast.

00:04:37.980 --> 00:04:39.780
So you can check out
that episode if you like,

00:04:39.780 --> 00:04:42.030
but studies done in her laboratory point

00:04:42.030 --> 00:04:44.760
to the fact that a daily,
very brief, in fact,

00:04:44.760 --> 00:04:48.780
only 13 minute meditation
can vastly increase

00:04:48.780 --> 00:04:50.460
focus and focus ability,

00:04:50.460 --> 00:04:53.610
not just immediately after
the meditation practice,

00:04:53.610 --> 00:04:55.680
but at all other times as well.

00:04:55.680 --> 00:04:56.513
So again,

00:04:56.513 --> 00:04:58.620
this is a meditation practice done daily

00:04:58.620 --> 00:04:59.700
for just 13 minutes.

00:04:59.700 --> 00:05:01.230
It's a very simple meditation practice

00:05:01.230 --> 00:05:02.700
where one sits or lies down,

00:05:02.700 --> 00:05:06.450
closes your eyes and
directs your attention

00:05:06.450 --> 00:05:09.780
to a place just between your
two eyes and right above it.

00:05:09.780 --> 00:05:10.613
So on your forehead.

00:05:10.613 --> 00:05:11.820
But just inside of that,

00:05:11.820 --> 00:05:13.590
and please understand that your brain

00:05:13.590 --> 00:05:14.850
does not have sensory receptors.

00:05:14.850 --> 00:05:16.740
So unlike focusing on your fingertips

00:05:16.740 --> 00:05:19.590
and the sensations there,
if you focus on your brain,

00:05:19.590 --> 00:05:20.970
you can't actually sense anything

00:05:20.970 --> 00:05:22.230
in your brain except your thoughts.

00:05:22.230 --> 00:05:25.410
So the idea then is that you
continually bring your focus

00:05:25.410 --> 00:05:28.110
back to that location just about an inch

00:05:28.110 --> 00:05:30.180
behind your forehead over and over again.

00:05:30.180 --> 00:05:32.610
And it's the refocusing of your attention

00:05:32.610 --> 00:05:34.290
to that location after it drifts

00:05:34.290 --> 00:05:37.320
that succeeds in increasing
your focus ability, again,

00:05:37.320 --> 00:05:39.300
not just during the
meditation and afterward,

00:05:39.300 --> 00:05:40.920
but at other times as well.

00:05:40.920 --> 00:05:43.680
So this 13 minute a day
meditation is exceedingly simple

00:05:43.680 --> 00:05:45.510
and exceedingly effective.

00:05:45.510 --> 00:05:46.950
It should be performed every day,

00:05:46.950 --> 00:05:49.050
but if you miss a day,
just go back to doing it.

00:05:49.050 --> 00:05:50.430
Don't despair too much.

00:05:50.430 --> 00:05:52.800
And you will see these
positive effects, say the data.

00:05:52.800 --> 00:05:55.110
Also increase effects on mood and other

00:05:55.110 --> 00:05:57.390
positive aspects of mental
health and performance.

00:05:57.390 --> 00:05:59.160
So that's the first tool in protocol.

00:05:59.160 --> 00:06:01.860
The second tool in protocol
relates to the general

00:06:01.860 --> 00:06:04.710
what I called arrow model of focus.

00:06:04.710 --> 00:06:07.470
This was a model that I created
in order to simplify the

00:06:07.470 --> 00:06:10.020
vast amounts of data on
focus and concentration

00:06:10.020 --> 00:06:11.100
and how they are created

00:06:11.100 --> 00:06:14.070
by the various chemical
systems within your brain.

00:06:14.070 --> 00:06:16.110
We're going to hear a lot about
these chemical systems again

00:06:16.110 --> 00:06:19.440
today in the context of nicotine
and they are as follows.

00:06:19.440 --> 00:06:20.970
You can think about focus

00:06:20.970 --> 00:06:24.000
on any goal or any endeavor as an arrow.

00:06:24.000 --> 00:06:26.130
So just imagine an arrow
which has an arrow head

00:06:26.130 --> 00:06:27.810
and a shaft, and we'll
add a third component

00:06:27.810 --> 00:06:28.713
to it in a moment.

00:06:29.880 --> 00:06:31.170
The head of the arrow,

00:06:31.170 --> 00:06:32.700
meaning the direction of your focus,

00:06:32.700 --> 00:06:35.190
is largely set by acetylcholine,

00:06:35.190 --> 00:06:36.690
which is a chemical in the brain.

00:06:36.690 --> 00:06:39.780
The shaft of the arrow
is set by a chemical

00:06:39.780 --> 00:06:42.600
called adrenaline, also
called epinephrine.

00:06:42.600 --> 00:06:43.470
Those are the same thing.

00:06:43.470 --> 00:06:46.260
In the brain typically it's
referred to as epinephrine,

00:06:46.260 --> 00:06:47.280
and in the body,

00:06:47.280 --> 00:06:49.140
it's more commonly
referred to as adrenaline,

00:06:49.140 --> 00:06:51.060
but those are the same neurochemical.

00:06:51.060 --> 00:06:54.300
Epinephrine slash adrenaline
represents the shaft

00:06:54.300 --> 00:06:57.510
of the arrow and it's providing the energy

00:06:57.510 --> 00:06:59.220
for which to focus.

00:06:59.220 --> 00:07:00.600
And then we can put behind that arrow

00:07:00.600 --> 00:07:03.150
a little propeller or
a motor, if you like,

00:07:03.150 --> 00:07:04.950
and the propeller or motor in the context

00:07:04.950 --> 00:07:07.470
of this neurochemistry model is dopamine,

00:07:07.470 --> 00:07:09.180
which provides ongoing motivation.

00:07:09.180 --> 00:07:11.670
It pushes that arrow forward continually

00:07:11.670 --> 00:07:15.180
as you strive to focus
on a particular thing.

00:07:15.180 --> 00:07:16.740
This particular arrow model,

00:07:16.740 --> 00:07:19.680
that is your ability
to increase your focus,

00:07:19.680 --> 00:07:23.070
can be enhanced therefore
by increasing acetylcholine,

00:07:23.070 --> 00:07:26.700
epinephrine, and dopamine simultaneously.

00:07:26.700 --> 00:07:28.410
And there are a lot of
different ways to do that.

00:07:28.410 --> 00:07:29.910
But one of the more effective ways to do

00:07:29.910 --> 00:07:34.200
that via supplement protocols
is so-called Alpha GPC.

00:07:34.200 --> 00:07:38.820
Alpha GPC taken in 300
milligram form 10 to 30 minutes

00:07:38.820 --> 00:07:41.850
before a about of cognitive
work or a about of physical work

00:07:41.850 --> 00:07:44.760
will increase your focus by way
of increasing acetylcholine,

00:07:44.760 --> 00:07:48.033
and to some extent, increasing
epinephrine as well.

00:07:48.870 --> 00:07:51.210
The dopamine increase will
have to be achieved either

00:07:51.210 --> 00:07:53.190
through cognitive processing,

00:07:53.190 --> 00:07:54.870
that is telling yourself
you're doing a good job

00:07:54.870 --> 00:07:56.520
and moving forward because thoughts really

00:07:56.520 --> 00:07:58.590
do impact your levels of dopamine,

00:07:58.590 --> 00:08:01.680
or some other sort of
pro dopamine or dopamine

00:08:01.680 --> 00:08:05.160
increasing protocol also
discussed in the toolkit for focus

00:08:05.160 --> 00:08:08.070
and our episode on dopamine
for motivation and drive.

00:08:08.070 --> 00:08:10.410
So the key thing here to
understand is that the 13 minute

00:08:10.410 --> 00:08:12.480
a day meditation is a very effective way

00:08:12.480 --> 00:08:14.220
to increase focus capacity.

00:08:14.220 --> 00:08:15.480
And then in the short term,

00:08:15.480 --> 00:08:18.630
if you want to provide a
boost now and again to focus,

00:08:18.630 --> 00:08:21.390
300 milligrams of Alpha
GPC can be very effective.

00:08:21.390 --> 00:08:22.413
There are various sources for that

00:08:22.413 --> 00:08:26.070
that we'll link to one of them
in the show note captions.

00:08:26.070 --> 00:08:28.770
By no means am I saying that
you need to take alpha GPC.

00:08:28.770 --> 00:08:30.780
A number of people will
certainly opt not to.

00:08:30.780 --> 00:08:33.210
And a number of people
might be saying, well,

00:08:33.210 --> 00:08:35.820
I've heard that Alpha GPC
can increase focus by way of

00:08:35.820 --> 00:08:39.090
increasing acetylcholine and
norepinephrine or epinephrine,

00:08:39.090 --> 00:08:41.100
but it can also increase TMAO,

00:08:41.100 --> 00:08:44.190
which is a kind of a negative
marker of cardiac health

00:08:44.190 --> 00:08:45.690
and cardiovascular health.

00:08:45.690 --> 00:08:49.020
For that reason, I and many
others will take 600 milligrams

00:08:49.020 --> 00:08:53.370
of a garlic capsule, which
can offset that TMAO increase.

00:08:53.370 --> 00:08:55.140
It remains uncertain as to how much

00:08:55.140 --> 00:08:58.620
Alpha GPC one needs to
take before increasing TMAO

00:08:58.620 --> 00:09:00.690
levels to a point where it's of concern

00:09:00.690 --> 00:09:02.790
that you would even need
to take the garlic capsule.

00:09:02.790 --> 00:09:04.560
But I just mention it in any case,

00:09:04.560 --> 00:09:06.330
because it's a pretty simple fix.

00:09:06.330 --> 00:09:08.760
Garlic has other health
benefits too, of course,

00:09:08.760 --> 00:09:10.200
and for most people,

00:09:10.200 --> 00:09:13.260
300 milligrams of Alpha GPC
taken every once in a while.

00:09:13.260 --> 00:09:14.660
I certainly don't encourage people

00:09:14.660 --> 00:09:17.349
to take Alpha GPC every
time they want to focus.

00:09:17.349 --> 00:09:20.610
I always emphasize behavioral tools first,

00:09:20.610 --> 00:09:24.300
then focusing on nutritional
tools and on occasion using

00:09:24.300 --> 00:09:26.910
supplement based tools to encourage

00:09:26.910 --> 00:09:29.040
increased levels of focus.

00:09:29.040 --> 00:09:31.260
And then of course there are a various

00:09:31.260 --> 00:09:33.930
number of different prescription compounds

00:09:33.930 --> 00:09:36.150
that if you're working with
a board certified physician,

00:09:36.150 --> 00:09:36.983
they could prescribe you

00:09:36.983 --> 00:09:40.080
if you need additional tools
for focus, things like Ritalin,

00:09:40.080 --> 00:09:43.170
Adderall, Modafinil,
Armodafinil, Vyvanse, et cetera,

00:09:43.170 --> 00:09:45.510
for many people are going to
be important and maybe even

00:09:45.510 --> 00:09:48.120
necessary for people with ADHD, et cetera,

00:09:48.120 --> 00:09:49.467
but that's a category into itself.

00:09:49.467 --> 00:09:50.460
And as I always say,

00:09:50.460 --> 00:09:52.740
I'm not a physician, so I
don't prescribe anything.

00:09:52.740 --> 00:09:55.503
I'm a professor, so I profess many things.

00:09:56.389 --> 00:09:58.470
And today I just wanted to
pass along or redirect your

00:09:58.470 --> 00:10:01.530
attention to that episode on focus

00:10:01.530 --> 00:10:02.850
and highlight those two tools,

00:10:02.850 --> 00:10:04.770
the 13 minute a day meditation,

00:10:04.770 --> 00:10:08.760
and 300 milligram Alpha GPC
for increasing focus capacity

00:10:08.760 --> 00:10:10.320
and for acutely,

00:10:10.320 --> 00:10:12.900
that is temporarily
giving an additional boost

00:10:12.900 --> 00:10:14.490
for a about of focus.

00:10:14.490 --> 00:10:17.100
And of course, if you choose
not to use those protocols,

00:10:17.100 --> 00:10:19.560
that's perfectly fine too,
there's certainly no obligation.

00:10:19.560 --> 00:10:20.790
They are simply available to you

00:10:20.790 --> 00:10:22.950
should you choose to try them.

00:10:22.950 --> 00:10:25.860
And if nothing else you now have in mind

00:10:25.860 --> 00:10:28.110
the neurochemistry of acetylcholine,

00:10:28.110 --> 00:10:30.480
epinephrine slash
adrenaline, and dopamine,

00:10:30.480 --> 00:10:33.390
and that will really set the
stage for understanding just

00:10:33.390 --> 00:10:36.170
how effective and why nicotine

00:10:36.170 --> 00:10:39.060
is so effective at
increasing focus, motivation,

00:10:39.060 --> 00:10:40.740
and even as you'll soon hear,

00:10:40.740 --> 00:10:42.840
working memory and cognitive capacity.

00:10:42.840 --> 00:10:43.800
Before we begin,

