00:32:11.820 --> 00:32:14.490
The second major effect that
nicotine has in the brain

00:32:14.490 --> 00:32:17.130
is that it increases acetylcholine.

00:32:17.130 --> 00:32:19.920
Acetylcholine is a
neuromodulator that exists in you

00:32:19.920 --> 00:32:23.580
and me, it is released from
multiple sites in the brain.

00:32:23.580 --> 00:32:27.450
And the two major sites
are the nucleus basalis,

00:32:27.450 --> 00:32:30.690
so these are a collection
of neurons in the front

00:32:30.690 --> 00:32:34.020
and base of your brain, and
from some brain stem areas.

00:32:34.020 --> 00:32:35.490
And there are a bunch of different ones

00:32:35.490 --> 00:32:36.690
back there in your brain stem,

00:32:36.690 --> 00:32:39.390
which is indeed in the back
that release acetylcholine

00:32:40.818 --> 00:32:42.450
that include the locus coeruleus
as kind of a minor site,

00:32:42.450 --> 00:32:44.340
the pedunculopontine nucleus.

00:32:44.340 --> 00:32:46.770
There are a bunch of
these different areas,

00:32:46.770 --> 00:32:48.270
that parabigeminal nucleus.

00:32:48.270 --> 00:32:49.830
There are a bunch of
these things back there.

00:32:49.830 --> 00:32:51.300
We don't have to go into all the names,

00:32:51.300 --> 00:32:53.760
but just understand that they're
little pockets of neurons,

00:32:53.760 --> 00:32:55.980
nerve cells located in
the front and the back

00:32:55.980 --> 00:32:57.540
and some extent in the
middle of your brain,

00:32:57.540 --> 00:32:59.460
but really in the front
and the back of your brain,

00:32:59.460 --> 00:33:03.990
that can serve two major
role, here they are.

00:33:03.990 --> 00:33:07.200
Acetylcholine released from
nucleus basalis leads to

00:33:07.200 --> 00:33:09.630
a sort of spotlighting or highlighting

00:33:09.630 --> 00:33:11.820
of particular neural
circuits in the brain.

00:33:11.820 --> 00:33:12.653
What do I mean by this?

00:33:12.653 --> 00:33:14.850
Well let's say you're working on a puzzle.

00:33:14.850 --> 00:33:15.960
Let's say it's a cognitive puzzle.

00:33:15.960 --> 00:33:17.580
Maybe you're doing a word puzzle,

00:33:17.580 --> 00:33:19.560
or nowadays I've heard
of this Wordle thing.

00:33:19.560 --> 00:33:21.030
I'm on Twitter and
people are always posting

00:33:21.030 --> 00:33:22.920
their Wordle thing and I
have no idea what it is,

00:33:22.920 --> 00:33:24.600
but I'm guessing it's some sort of puzzle.

00:33:24.600 --> 00:33:26.070
I'm guessing it's like a crossword puzzle,

00:33:26.070 --> 00:33:27.810
and here, if I'm wrong,
I don't know, educate me.

